Architecture — “AI-Powered Observability Stack”
----------------------------------------------------
Layers

Data Layer:

Logs: Cloud Logging, ELK, Datadog, Splunk

Metrics: Prometheus, Cloud Monitoring

Traces: OpenTelemetry, Jaeger

AI/ML Layer:

Anomaly detection models

Causal graph models for RCA

LLMs for log summarization and reasoning

Incident Intelligence Layer:

Correlation engine

Incident classification (severity, impact, owner)

Generative AI copilots for summaries

Response Automation Layer:

Integrations with ServiceNow, PagerDuty, Opsgenie

Automated runbooks (Cloud Functions, Lambda, GitOps actions)

Visualization Layer:

Dashboards (Grafana, Looker, Cloud Console)

ChatOps interfaces (Slack, Teams, Vertex AI Agent Chat)



--------------------------------------------------------------
| Category                        | Example                                                               |
| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Incident Summary Generation** | “Summarize the last 1 hour of alerts and probable root cause.”        |
| **ChatOps / Natural Queries**   | “Why is the latency of service X high since 9 PM?”                    |
| **RCA Automation**              | LLM uses context from logs + traces to identify faulty dependency.    |
| **Knowledge Graph Integration** | LLM references past incidents to recommend proven fixes.              |
| **Runbook Automation**          | Generate or execute Terraform/Ansible scripts to remediate incidents. |


